{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-recursive-brane-tower","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:recursive-brane-tower","kind":"definition","title":"Recursive Brane Tower","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-jet-prolongation"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-recursive-brane-tower-su2"],"tags":["brane-tower","jet-bundle","frobenius-hopf"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.RecursiveBraneTower","text":"recursive-brane-tower.md","leanSource":"recursive-brane-tower.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:recursive-brane-tower\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe over a ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> commutative; then every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(A_n)</code> is commutative as well. Set <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_0 = A</code> and inductively <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_{n+1} = T(A_n) = \\mathrm{Sym}_{A_n}(\\Omega^1_{A_n/R})</code>, the tangent algebra of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code> (<a href=\"#prop:jet-prolongation\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/jet-prolongation\">jet prolongation</a>), whose degree-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\le 1</code> part is the <a href=\"#def:categorical-jet\" data-at=\"quantum-universes/qu-structures\">jet object</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^1(A_n)</code>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>recursive brane tower</strong> is the sequence</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  A_0 \\hookrightarrow A_1 \\hookrightarrow A_2 \\hookrightarrow \\cdots</code></pre>\n<p>in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>, where each embedding is the structure map <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell_n \\colon A_n \\hookrightarrow T(A_n) = A_{n+1}</code>. The augmentation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r_n\\colon A_{n+1} \\to A_n</code>, which kills <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Omega^1_{A_n/R}</code>, satisfies <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r_n \\circ \\ell_n = \\mathrm{id}</code>, so each level is a direct summand of the next.</p>\n<p>The <em>brane relation</em> makes the structure recursive: each jet object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code> is the base object — the <em>brane</em> — of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_{n+1}</code>, and the comultiplication <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_n</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code> encodes the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th level connection. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A = \\mathcal{O}(G)</code> one has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n = \\mathcal{O}(T^n G)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_n</code> is the comultiplication of the iterated tangent group; a Frobenius form on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_n</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\ge 1</code>, is not required.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/recursive-brane-tower.md","heading":"Definition","number":"6.1.6","page":"b/def-recursive-brane-tower","qa":{"counts":{"pass":83,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.RecursiveBraneTower","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/recursive-brane-tower.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
